  ## A blocked-tail package restores the skip/allow indices after the ordinary
  ## tail package has hidden its existential failure kind.  It is constructed
  ## only from the blocked no-result constructor, so the later dispatcher can
  ## consume one canonical `AtomicStartSkipEvidence`/`AtomicStartAllowed` pair
  ## without guessing which candidate branch produced it.
  type AtomicStartBlockedTailPackage(depth: Nat, n: Nat, machine: PatternMachine(n)) indices (position: InitialPosition, input: List(Char), after_input: List(Char), history: List(Char), capture_context: List(EvidenceInstruction), policy: NewlinePolicy, prefix_mode: Bool, reversed_prefix: List(Char), whole: List(LookaroundAdmittedState(n)), current: List(LookaroundAdmittedState(n)))
