  ## Recursive commit tail with its cursor authority and exact structure kept
  ## in one relevant package. The cause remains erased but is explicit, so a
  ## proof consumer can forward that exact cause into another erased slot;
  ## the indexed structure still prevents pairing it with an unrelated cause
  ## or recovering a cursor from proof-only data.
  type AtomicPathCommitStructureCursorExistentialPackage(depth: Nat, n: Nat, machine: PatternMachine(n)) indices (input: List(Char), after_input: List(Char), state: ThreadState(n), history: List(Char), capture_context: List(EvidenceInstruction), policy: NewlinePolicy, scope_depth: Nat, prefix_mode: Bool, reversed_prefix: List(Char), whole: List(LookaroundAdmittedState(n)), current: List(LookaroundAdmittedState(n)), commit_depth: Nat, kind: AtomicPathCommitCauseKind)
    AtomicPathCommitStructureCursorExistentialPacked : (@erased cause: AtomicPathCommitCause(depth, n, machine, input, after_input, state, history, capture_context, policy, scope_depth, prefix_mode, reversed_prefix, whole, current, commit_depth, kind)) -> (cursor: LookaroundAdmittedStateCursorSuffixPackage(n, whole, current)) -> (structure: AtomicPathCommitStructurePackage(depth, n, machine, input, after_input, state, history, capture_context, policy, scope_depth, prefix_mode, reversed_prefix, whole, current, commit_depth, kind, cause)) -> AtomicPathCommitStructureCursorExistentialPackage(depth, n, machine, input, after_input, state, history, capture_context, policy, scope_depth, prefix_mode, reversed_prefix, whole, current, commit_depth, kind)

  ## Construction-time outer classification for a recursive commit structure.
  ## Every constructor retains the original cursor/structure existential at
  ## its exact kind while hiding the kind-specific indices from later callers.
